  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41160934",
      "title": "NextJS vs \"Just React\" - Analyzing The NextJS Project",
      "lectureOrder": 5,
      "videoOrder": 5,
      "sourceHash": "0229ce7c5c66b824f38e1ee2ca13dd1414d206ec977bb09057932e8eb61c2df7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "So we have this first starting project here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 7.65,
          "en": "and what's really important about this project is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.65,
          "end": 12.01,
          "en": "that if you inspect the page source in your browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.01,
          "end": 14.64,
          "en": "you'll see a bunch of code in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.64,
          "end": 17.433,
          "en": "But most importantly, if you take a closer look,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.435,
          "end": 20.13,
          "en": "you'll see the actual page content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.13,
          "end": 22.293,
          "en": "somewhere in that source code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "And that's important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "because that means that the actual content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 30.39,
          "en": "that's visible on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 35.39,
          "en": "so this text here in this case, was part of the HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.58,
          "end": 38.88,
          "en": "that was sent back from the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.88,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "And that's special because that's not the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 45.423,
          "en": "in a standard client site React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.091,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "There, if you inspect the source code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 53.58,
          "en": "you will just see basically empty page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "and some script imports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 57.78,
          "en": "but you won't see the actual content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.78,
          "end": 61.23,
          "en": "that's visible on the screen in that source code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.23,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 67.62,
          "en": "a standard React app is manipulated on the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.62,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "site in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 74.96000000000001,
          "en": "React.js by default is a client site JavaScript library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.3,
          "end": 78.21000000000001,
          "en": "which means it runs in the browser and it edits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.21000000000001,
          "end": 81.06,
          "en": "and manipulates the page in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.06,
          "end": 82.26,
          "en": "And that's amazing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.26,
          "end": 85.05,
          "en": "because that means that the page can be edited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.05,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "after it's been loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "We can update the state of that page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 93.063,
          "en": "after it's been loaded without having to fetch a new page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.96000000000001,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "But the disadvantage is that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 101.00999999999999,
          "en": "search engine crawlers don't see the actual page content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.00999999999999,
          "end": 103.833,
          "en": "if they visit the page for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "And that's the difference here with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "Here, we got all the content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 112.02000000000001,
          "en": "not just visually on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.02000000000001,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "but in the actual source code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "Because with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 119.94,
          "en": "you no longer have a client-side application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.94,
          "end": 123.27,
          "en": "Instead you have a full stack application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.27,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "with NextJS projects, you have code that runs on the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 130.44,
          "en": "and you have a lot of code that runs on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 133.02,
          "en": "NextJS simply is both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 137.22,
          "en": "It's not just client-side, not just backend, it's both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.22,
          "end": 140.94,
          "en": "And NextJS seamlessly blends client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.94,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "and server-side so that you can use React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 146.34,
          "en": "to build amazing full stack applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.34,
          "end": 148.113,
          "en": "And that's what we'll do now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
